  "term": "causalgia",
  "definition": "Causalgia is a type of complex regional pain syndrome in which an injured peripheral nerve leads to burning pain and unusually strong sensitivity to touch in that nerve’s distribution. It can also involve autonomic changes such as altered sweating, blood vessel regulation, and skin nutrition changes.",
